From e7b853e8252716e6fa43e17bcfb05c5a008a7711 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: iitimii <timiiowolabi@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 22:05:20 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 20/24] S1b: llama-residency module, verbs, ledger, selftest

Weight residency manager for streamed loads: per-unit range tables built
from tensors_by_name, pin/prefetch/evict verbs on a single background
thread, a two-step head-aware ledger, the ring/window state machine and a
selftest that asserts the invariants on real memory counters.

- src/llama-residency.{h,cpp}: unit table (one unit per blk.N, one for the
  tied head, one always-pinned misc unit), sorted+merged byte ranges,
  runtime sysconf(_SC_PAGESIZE), inward alignment for evict and outward for
  prefetch. Verbs run only on the manager thread (mutex + condition
  variable + FIFO deque, atomic per-unit state for dedupe); the module owns
  its own O_RDONLY fd. evict = llama_mmap::discard_range then
  fadvise_discard per range, in that order. prefetch = MADV_NORMAL +
  chunked MADV_WILLNEED hints, then the touch loop that is the actual
  mechanism and the completion signal.
- Ledger: head-pinned config first, head-streamed only if that is
  infeasible, W reduced toward 1 before refusing; b_layer_max over the
  streamed layers is solved to a fixed point. Refusal prints the failing
  inequality with numbers and returns NULL.
- llama_residency_on_gate_post() (internal) evicts every resident streamed
  unit outside [u, u+W] and queues the window ahead of the cursor. The
  public cb_eval is a stub for now: ASK -> false, POST -> true. Graph
  gating lands in S2/B3.
- src/llama-model.{h,cpp}: new llama_model::mappings() accessor; extra
  buffer types are disabled for streamed loads, since repacking copies
  weights out of the mapping into anonymous memory where they can be
  neither evicted nor faulted back in.
- common: build the manager between model load and context creation,
  install cb_eval, free it before the model; --residency-selftest reports
  PASS/FAIL and exits; an unset context size is pinned to the -fit floor so
  a RAM budget is not blown by the model's full training context.

Assisted-by: Claude Fable 5
